Have an LLB or equivalent degree.
Admission as Attorney and experience in legal practice is advantageous.
Must have a minimum of at least 2 years (post qualification) exposure to a legal practice or in-house legal department dealing primarily with general commercial work/drafting and vetting of a wide variety of contracts of the nature described above.
A sound knowledge of legislation impacting the above business lines
Experience in litigation and Intellectual Property will be advantageous.
Excellent analytical skills with attention to detail, logical thought processes and sound judgment and decision-making abilities.
Excellent organisational, planning and prioritising skills.

