Job Description
At Truworths, you'll find a dynamic business manufacturing environment where our staff is constantly challenged to reinvent the way we do business in order to keep us at the forefront of the South African fashion industry.
Truworths currently has an exciting opportunity for a Grader in our Manufacturing division.
The position is based at our Truworths Head Office in Cape Town.
Key Responsibilities
Liaising with the Merchandisers Planners, Designers, Garments Technologists and Design Room Manager;
To alter patterns on the Gerber system;
Grade patterns on the Gerber system and produce in line with the production critical path;
Pattern Digitising and creating production spec sheets;
To produce markers in the most accurate and cost effective manner in line with the production critical path;
Prioritise styles for grading in line with production plan;
Liaising with the Department Head.
Qualifications and Experience
Must have 5 years’ experience using Gerber;
Minimum 1-2 years’ experience in similar role;
Must have experience of working with fashion outerwear and Tailoring;
Gerber and grading knowledge is needed.
Competencies
Able to work successfully within a team to meet tight deadlines
Excellent communication and organisational skills
Deadline:31st August,2026
go to method of application »

RESPONSIBILITIES AND OBLIGATIONS
The primary responsibility of the Facilities Administrator is to deliver a smooth functioning facilities administration. In pursuance of this primary responsibility, the Facilities Administrator is required to:
Control use and storage of movable assets;
Assume driver’s responsibilities when on leave;
Assume reception responsibilities;
Ordering of authorised furniture;
Ordering of authorised office equipment and maintenance of printing machines;
Ordering and control of Printing paper;
Ordering stationery for new employees;
Ordering of groceries and refreshments;
Making use of checklists for all office management activities;
Create requisitions on Oracle and follow up on payment for suppliers;
Constant interaction with Office Assistants and the driver;
Monitor and guide suppliers when they deliver service within the building;
Mail Management – outgoing;
Control use and safekeeping of company vehicles and maintenance thereof (service, tyre changes, fines are paid etc);
When required collect and deliver company postage.
Added Responsibilities
Interact with other programmes;
Administer office space Management;
Interact with CMMS on maintenance lodged by tenants or programmes;
Interact with Service Providers e.g Canteen, Printing, Grass Cutting etc;
Provide Monthly reports on Facilities and Office Admin related matters;
Understands Safety, Health & Environment.
EXPECTED OUTCOMES
The CDC offices run smoothly on a day to day basis;
Reduction of overhead costs;
Company vehicles and booking systems are well maintained;
Movable assets under the control of office management are properly managed;
Groceries, refreshments and stationery stock levels are maintained;
Furniture is received in good order and timeously as and when required;
New employees receive all necessary equipment upon arrival;
Ensure that invoices received from Finance for authorisation are returned to Finance speedily to ensure that payments are made on time;
Understand CDC systems- Oracle, CMMS, Timesheet etc
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS
National Diploma in Office Management or any other related field of study;
Minimum of 3 years’ experience in an office management environment;
Good computer skills and communication skills;
Valid driver’s license.

Minimum Requirements:
Grade 12 certificate. Computer Literacy. Undergo 21 days data capture training.
The curriculum for the course (both theory and practical) is in such a manner that it leads to the personal and professional development of a data capture so that, on completion of the course he/she should:
Duties:
Ensure patient’s records and files are properly kept and secured; Reconcile patients’ records with various registers;
ensure ongoing data capturing from patient records in to the database with high standards of accuracy;
identify, resolve or query missing data and errors observed during data entry, electronic checks or manual review;
report missing data and errors to the manager at the facility; review and validate all data from the patient records to ensure all data is correct, complete and logical; communicate and distribute data to the facility.
