The successful candidate will be responsible for managing day-to-day transaction execution, leading financial modelling and analysis, supporting client delivery, coordinating stakeholders and contributing to business development initiatives. The role requires a high degree of independence, strong technical capability and a genuine interest in the infrastructure sector.
Qualifications / Certifications required:
CA(SA), CFA or finance-related bachelor’s degree
Financial modelling certification beneficial
Experience required:
3-5 years project finance experience
Experience in project finance advisory, infrastructure transactions, debt raising, refinancing and/or PPP transactions
Experience across energy, water, and transport sectors
Responsibilities of role:
The successful candidate will have an execution-focused project finance dealmaker role within the team and be responsible for the following activities on a day-to-day basis:
Project Management
Manage multiple workstreams and engagements to ensure deadlines are met with accuracy and efficiency;
Coordinate with client teams, providers of finance, legal advisers and other project stakeholders to ensure efficient workflow;
Take ownership of day-to-day transaction execution; and
Support senior team members in managing overall engagement delivery.
Financial Modelling
Build financial models based on industry best practice;
Translate requirements of project agreements into the financial models;
Develop realistic scenarios and sensitivity analysis and interpretation thereof in the context of the project;
Run sensitivities for investors and lenders as required;
Prepare outputs and analysis for investors, lenders and clients as required; and
Coordinate with model auditors to ensure structural integrity, tax and accounting compliance.
Project Finance
Demonstrate a sound understanding of limited recourse funding structures;
Demonstrate an understanding of the infrastructure market and a strong interest in developing sector specialisation;
Demonstrate an understanding of public-private partnerships;
Support / advise clients in raising finance for infrastructure projects;
Prepare necessary project marketing materials including but not limited to information memoranda, teasers etc., as well as other materials for potential investors and lenders;
Support the preparation and negotiation of term sheets; and
Review and analyse commercial agreements and financing documentation.
Infrastructure mergers and acquisitions
Leading the compilation of key transaction documentation including teasers, information memoranda, management presentations, bid documentation and investment committee papers.
Support clients on acquisition, disposal and strategic review mandates in the infrastructure sector; and
Manage due diligence processes and coordinate input from relevant internal and external stakeholders.
Proposals
Prepare proposals and pitch materials;
Support and manage internal risk assessments, compliance processes and engagement setup; and
Contribute to business development initiatives and market research.
Team Contribution
Supervise, support and review the work of associates and junior team members;
Contribute to a collaborative and high-performing team environment; and
Support knowledge sharing and capability development within the team.
Skill sets required:
Advanced Excel skills;
Financial modelling skills;
Awareness of AI capabilities and a drive for improving efficiency;
Good interpersonal and client relationship skills;
Problem solving capabilities;
Attention to detail and an ability to perform critical self-review of outputs;
A desire to build on commercial and industry knowledge;
Negotiation skills;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills are essential, including the ability to write succinct, well-structured reports and client communications;
Passion for the development of South Africa and the African continent;
A well-organised and self-directed individual who can relate to people at all levels of an organisation;
Proven ability to multitask and ensure effective delivery of the priorities to meet targets and objectives (strong time management skills);
Ability to run independently with projects when necessary;
Project and client management skill;
Conflict management skill;
Thrive in an unstructured environment where each day is different;
A highly motivated, confident individual with presence;
Highly rated with strong academic credentials; and
A proactive and dynamic team player, who works effectively under pressure.

Areas of Responsibility
In this role, the Case Assistant will use their newly obtained knowledge in the related field, to sell the full range of Cook Peripheral Interventional, Cook Interventional Radiology, Cook Embolisation, Angiodynamics Oncology, Getinge, Varian, and Cardionovum products in a professional manner by calling on health care professionals and related role players i.e., Vascular surgeons, Interventional Radiologists, Stock Controllers, Theatre staff etc.
The Case Assistant will be expected to maintain current business, by creating relationships with customers, in the shortest time, and service current business thereby.
Maintaining existing business in the assigned territory;
Scheduling and attending appointments with existing customers
Preparing stock for and attending theatre lists, to service the product related needs of the customers;
Completion of weekly planner and activity report for submission to direct manager;
Responsible for networking with and managing existing customers;
Counting and management of consignment stock;
Requesting and following up on quotations;
General administration associated with the position.
Clear responsibility and accountability of the abovementioned SBU’s
Administrative Duties:
Adhere to credit policies and procedures of the group;
Maintain all administrative responsibilities associated with this position; monthly reporting on marketing activities;
Ensure all product and marketing activities comply with legal and ethical standards;
Managing all company expenses within the marketing budget provided;
Adhere to any legal or medical requirements and inform management of changed requirements;
Submit monthly reports to management.
Stock Management:
Assist with stock rotation and slow-moving identification and returns;
Assist Sales Manager with input from the field on stock ordering and give feedback on stock requirements from the field;
Management of consignment stock allocated to customers on request from Sales Manager;
Management of boot stock allocated and rotation of stock when needed to reduce unnecessary expiration of products;
Giving feedback to Management on consignment stock.
Requirements
Qualifications
A relevant degree is a minimum requirement;
Any medical and marketing qualifications would be a definite advantage.
Additional Requirements
Preference will be given to a candidate residing in the KZN region.
Own reliable vehicle with travel in the KZN region, even after hours;
Someone wanting to gain much-needed experience in this Medical Sales Industry;
Willingness to work hard and long hours when required.
Experience Required
Medical experience during education is a preference and previous experience in a similar position such as Vascular or any experience in the Medical Industry would be an advantage;
Knowledge of the target group of customers will be an advantage;
Computer literacy and proficiency on MS Office, specifically Excel (level 2 at least) and MS Word is a requirement for this position;
Clinical and product knowledge will be a definite advantage.
Skills/Competencies
Advanced planning and organizational skills;
Excellent written & verbal communication skills;
Strong analytical, organizational and decision-making skills;
Ability to work independently and as a team member, while using discretion in decision making and sound judgment in problem solving;
Demonstrated follow-through, initiative, attention to detail and drive for continuous improvement;
High level of energy and stress tolerance required;
Ability to work well under pressure and maintain positive, enthusiastic attitude;
High level of motivation and vision and results orientated;
Ability to work effectively in a team environment and build strong working relationships;
Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and meet deadlines;
Time management to be efficient;
Strong work ethics;
Proficient in Microsoft Office – specially Excel and PowerPoint Outlook;
Integrity, responsive, high commitment;
Desire to win with a drive on results.
Benefits
Basic and Travel Allowance
50% medical Aid and Provident Fund
Fuel Card, Laptop, Cell and Data Allowance (Reimbursed) of R1300 per month
