The successful candidate will be responsible for the following key performance areas:
Review, analyse and evaluate regulated institutions (banks and insurers) with regard to Pillar 3 Disclosures.
Review and evaluate financial entities’ disclosure process for compliance with legislation requirements.
Analyse and interpret risk-based regulatory returns and reconcile them with the Pillar 3 reported disclosures for regulated entities.
Conduct research and provide input into the regulatory framework (e.g. the Banks Act 94 of 1990, Insurance Act 18 of 2017), in line with international best practice.
Interpret and develop amendments to the legislative framework, including the development of regulatory instruments (directives and standards), based on international best practices.
Contribute towards the international and local Disclosure framework working committees.
Contribute to the development and implementation of the supervisory review and evaluation process in respect of Pillar 3, in line with international best practice.
Develop and implement the supervisory framework in relation to Pillar 3 Disclosures for banking and insurance.
Report on the compliance of the entities to the Pillar 3 legislation.
Job requirements
To be considered for this position, candidates must be in possession of:
a postgraduate qualification (NQF 8) specialising in Accounting, Auditing, Banking, Insurance, Finance, or Risk Management; and
at least two to five years’ experience in the finance sector or risk management environment.
The following would be an added advantage:
a Chartered Accountant (CA(SA)) qualification;
being a Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA)
being a Financial Risk Manager (FRM);
membership of the Actuarial Society of South Africa (ASSA); and
practical experience in a financial and/or business environment.
Additional requirements include:
knowledge of and experience in financial, banking or insurance products, regulations or risk models;
being conversant in the second Pillar of the Basel III framework at both theoretical and practical levels;
keeping abreast of best practice in capital management;
an understanding of the Basel III framework regarding the definition of capital and leverage ratio;
